	(gr_text "Planes & Power: Establish your 6V, 5V, and 3.3V planes/polygons.\n\nMCU Stability: VCL and Decoupling caps.\n\nClocks: Shortest possible paths.\n\nHigh-Speed: Raspberry Pi 5 signals.\n\nHigh-Current: Motor driver power and PWM.\n\nSensitive Signal: Sonar Echo/Analog lines.\n\nGeneral: PMODs and LEDs."
		(at 297.18 -27.94 0)
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "68afdee8-d6c0-49ea-9ed3-c0288e20a095")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "L1	Top	High-Current Power: VM, OUT1, OUT2, and Buck Switching Node.\nL2	Inner 1	Solid Ground (GND): No routing here. This is your shield and heat sink.\nL3	Inner 2	Low-Voltage Power: Buck Output (3.3V/5V) and VM distribution.\nL4	Bottom	Signal Routing: PWM, SPI, Chip Select, nFAULT, and IPROPI."
		(at 281.94 25.4 0)
		(layer "Dwgs.User")
		(uuid "a2335931-011c-45c1-b987-ca1aed686941")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "The Most Important Traces (Priority Order)\nD+ / D- (Differential Pair): These must stay together. If one trace is longer or wider than the other, the data becomes garbled.\n\nCC1 / CC2 (Configuration Channels): These tell the charger what voltage to send. If these fail, you get 0V or a slow 5V charge.\n\nVBUS / GND (Power): These carry the high current (up to 3A or 5A). They need to be wide."
		(at -40.64 137.16 0)
		(layer "Dwgs.User")
		(uuid "faa5358f-58ca-4c15-b920-a4bec4f921a6")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
				(thickness 0.15)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
